Description: Show 3D films in 3D: one view per eye in a stereo GtkGLArea, the input corrections, the save into the file
 Celluloid's video area becomes a stereo GtkGLArea for a film whose frames
 hold two views (libmpv's MPV_RENDER_PARAM_STEREO_VIEW says so): each view is
 rendered once, at the size libmpv gives so that nothing is resized before the
 compositor, and the area declares the pair as full side by side stereo
 content. A 2D film is rendered as before.
 The menu gains "3D" with the edition's options and no others: Enable 3D,
 3D Input Format (the stereo layer's list, offered for a film shown in 3D or
 whose picture is found to be a pair), Swap left and right eyes and Save the
 correction into the file (for a film shown in 3D), Display Settings.
 A correction is kept where Celluloid keeps the film's resume position
 (mpv's watch-later entry, video-stereo-input and video-stereo-swap), and the
 film's file is written only when the person chooses the save (libstereo-av:
 Matroska StereoMode, MP4 st3d, read back); the entry's correction is then
 cleared. A film that cannot be shown per eye is shown flat, left view alone,
 and the person is told once; a film without an audio track says "This film
 has no sound.". The window fits one view of a pair. The new sentences are in
 the nine catalogues of the edition's languages, the menu's words taken from
 the stereo layer's catalogues.
 Upstream does not take changes written with AI assistance (its README), so
 this is the edition's patch and is not offered.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: other, Sparky Stereo OS (queue row 137, milestone 3)
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-25
---
